  "slug": "biclustering-convex-aed0",
  "summary": "Sequence and single-cell foundation models now predict regulatory variant effects and networks, with parameter-efficient transfer to new contexts.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reusable representations learned from large genomic and transcriptomic data and then adapted to regulatory and variant tasks. ChromBERT pretrains on ChIP-seq from about 1,000 transcription regulators to learn interpretable, context-specific regulatory networks, while AlphaGenome predicts thousands of functional genomic tracks at base-pair resolution from 1 Mb of sequence. Downstream adaptation is becoming cheaper: parameter-efficient fine-tuning transfers Borzoi to new cell types and assays while reducing runtime. Interpretability is a parallel focus, with scGeneLens applying sparse block attention, attention propagation, and integrated gradients to single-cell foundation models, and Volaria building gene-centered representations that integrate coding and regulatory variants. DeepCE and KGBN are less representation-centric, addressing network inference and knowledge-graph-augmented logical models. The newer element is the shift toward transfer efficiency and mechanistic dissection of what these models have learned.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-31"
}
